  "sections": {
    "1": {
      "purpose": "This System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem of [Project Name].  The purpose of this software is to acquire and process real-time telemetry data from various sensor channels, enabling critical mission operations in a defense environment. The system will support existing parent systems by providing reliable and timely access to critical operational data. This SRS is intended for use by developers, engineers, testers, and other stakeholders involved in the development and deployment of this software.",
      "scope": "Introduction\n\nThis System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem of the [Project Name] R&D software project.\n\nIn Scope:\n\nAcquisition and Processing of Telemetry Data: The system shall acquire telemetry data from at least three sensor channels simultaneously.\nTimestamping: The system shall timestamp every acquired sample with a system time reference accurate to +/- 1 ms.\nBuffering: The system shall buffer at least 10,000 samples per channel before flow control is applied. This requirement refines REQ-0003 by requiring bounded buffering for time-tagged data.\nREST Interface: The system shall expose acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment.\nEngineering Log: The system shall record an engineering log with a minimum depth of 6 months of mission operations.\nSystem Reliability and Performance:  The system shall have a mean time between failures (MTBF) of not less than 2000 hours, sustain a sample ingestion rate of at least 100 Hz per channel, restrict access to acquisition controls to authenticated operators only, complete a software restart in less than 30 seconds after a fault.\nPower Envelope: The system shall operate within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W.\n\nOut of Scope:\n\nThis SRS does not define the detailed design or implementation of the telemetry acquisition subsystem, including specific sensor types, data processing algorithms, or REST API implementation details.\nThis SRS does not cover the integration of the telemetry acquisition subsystem with other systems within the [Project Name] R&D software project.",
