    "2": {
      "system_context": "System Overview\n\nSystem Boundaries:\n\nThe system under development is responsible for acquiring, timestamping, buffering, and transmitting telemetry data from at least three sensor channels.  It interfaces with the ground segment via a REST interface to provide access to acquired samples. The system also maintains an engineering log of mission operations for at least six months.\n\nExternal Interfaces:\n\nGround Segment: The system exposes acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment, enabling data transfer and analysis.\nEngineering Log: The system records an engineering log with a minimum depth of six months of mission operation data. This log serves as a historical record for troubleshooting and operational analysis.\nPower Source: The system operates within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W, ensuring efficient power consumption and reliable operation.\n\nSystem Context:\n\nThe system operates in a controlled environment with defined boundaries to ensure data integrity and security. Access to acquisition controls is restricted to authenticated operators only, preventing unauthorized manipulation of the system. The system's Mean Time Between Failures (MTBF) must be not less than 2000 hours, ensuring continuous operation and minimizing downtime.  The system achieves a sample ingestion rate of at least 100 Hz per channel, enabling real-time data processing and analysis.\n\nSource: REQ-0001, REQ-0003, REQ-0004, REQ-0005, REQ-0006, REQ-0007, REQ-0008, REQ-0009, REQ-0010\n\nNote: This document provides a high-level overview of the system's boundaries and external interfaces. Further details regarding specific functionalities and interactions will be provided in subsequent sections of this specification.",
      "system_architecture": "System Overview\n\nThe system is designed to acquire telemetry data from multiple sensor channels simultaneously and timestamp each sample with high accuracy.  It will buffer samples before flow control, ensuring reliable data delivery even under high-demand conditions. The system provides a REST interface for accessing acquired data and maintains a detailed engineering log of mission operations.\n\nKey Architectural Components:\n\nSensor Acquisition Module: Acquires telemetry data from multiple sensor channels.\nData Buffering Module:  Buffers acquired samples before flow control to maintain real-time data delivery.\nTimestamping Module: Timestamps each acquired sample with high accuracy.\nREST Interface Module: Exposes acquired data through a REST interface for ground segment access.\nEngineering Log Module: Records an engineering log of mission operations, maintaining at least six months of historical data.\nPower Management Module:  Operates within a 28 V DC power envelope not exceeding 45 W.\n\nNote: Detailed design information is provided in the System Design Document (SDD).",
